{"seq":14,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/qm-pi-sonnet-none-mu-memory/ms-08-saltmarsh-summary/r5","wall_ts":"2026-10-26T22:35:01.828Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"599d57917dda2c7e99193eae35a143dc2798f17eefab594447e0575a4dc6506a","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","text":"Sofia, I could confirm two of the three. The handover answer is only partly supported.\n\n1. **Who took over and when:** Moss's Coastal notes say Saltmarsh Provisions was due to change hands on Monday, 6 October 2025. They don't name the new owner. Several things point to Bettina Kroll:\n   - Bettina handles Saltmarsh in #coastal-team.\n   - On 17 November she called it \"Sofia's old grocery account\".\n   - Moss's 18 May coverage note calls it \"Bettina's grocery account\".\n\n   None of these says outright that she took it over, so please confirm the name with Bettina or Ruth before it goes in the handover file.\n2. **Discount:** It is 10%. On 17 November 2025, Bettina first posted 12%, then corrected it within minutes to 10%. She said she had misread June Osei-Lark's draft worksheet.\n3. **Corinne's admin access ticket:** PD-4827. Kwame opened it on 15 October 2025. Corinne's admin option had disappeared, but she could still sign in.\n\nMoss's notes also mention PD-4824. That is a separate ticket, about door 3 to door 4 moves showing as missed appointments."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C1253QW9NJ6","ts":"1791986400.000124"}}
